# notes cv v cv2
he terms "opencv" and "opencv2" in C++ code often refer to different ways of including the OpenCV library, specifically related to the older C-style interface versus the newer C++ interface.
Opencv (Older C-style Interface)
In older versions of OpenCV or when using the C interface, you might see includes like this:
#C++
#include "opencv/cv.h"
#include "opencv/highgui.h"
#include "opencv/cxcore.h"
These headers correspond to the older C-style API of OpenCV. While still functional, this approach is less common in modern C++ OpenCV development.
Opencv2 (Newer C++ Interface)
The "opencv2" directory contains the headers for the modern C++ interface of OpenCV. The includes would look like this:
# C++
#include <opencv2/core.hpp>
#include <opencv2/imgproc.hpp>
#include <opencv2/highgui.hpp>
#include <opencv2/features2d.hpp>
// ... other modules as needed
